I think I got this from delphi, but its been repacked with a coco versionadded to the archive. Gene Heskett <gene_heskett@wvlink.mpl.com>  Thanks to Tim Kientzle for permission to release his code BEFORE thepublish date of Sept. 1995 in Dr. Dobb's Journal.  This archive contains:       mime.readme - this file       mimecode.c  - C source for 68000 OS-9       mimecode070 - binary file compiled on a mm/1 68070 with                     Microware C version 3.2       mimecode809 - binary file compiled on a CoCo3 6309 with                     MicroWare C version 1.00+ for OS9 levels 1-2                     This version added by Gene Heskett, this code                     compiled on my machine with no errors as is.  To install: Rename the correct version for your machine to remove              the 070 or 809 extension, then move to the cmds dir.              You might have to adjust the attributes after the move              methods I used "adjust" them.  To use: mimecode [-option] <anyfile >newfile                    -e encode                    -d decode                    -? list options  So now you can go after those mime base64 files on the 'net.  Thanks Tim!